In `--brief` mode, collapse to one line:

```
ITS-XXX  [In Review]  PR #1234 green  worktree clean  ✓ ready to merge
ITS-YYY  [In Progress]  no PR yet  worktree dirty (3 files)  — keep working
ITS-ZZZ  [Triage]  ⚠ blocked by ENG-101
```

## Composite "Attention" rules

The `⚠ Attention` line is computed from the gathered data — surface the most important one signal:

| Condition | Attention line |
|---|---|
| Open PR has `mergeable: CONFLICTING` | "PR has conflicts — run /shopstack-conflict-resolver" |
| Open PR has `reviewDecision: CHANGES_REQUESTED` | "Reviewer requested changes — address before merging" |
| Open PR has CI failed | "CI failed on step <name> — check the run" |
| Open PR has been open >7 days with no activity | "PR stale (>7d) — bump or rebase" |
| Worktree is dirty AND last commit is >24h old | "Worktree has uncommitted changes from yesterday" |
| Ticket is In Progress but no worktree exists | "Linear says In Progress but no local worktree — orphan claim?" |
| Ticket has unresolved dep in `Triage` | "Blocked by <dep> still in Triage" |
| Lessons has ≥3 recent escalations on this ticket | "Repeated escalations — may be structural" |
| None of the above | (omit the line) |

## Hard rules

- **Read-only.** This skill makes no mutations — no Linear state changes, no git commits, no PR edits.
- **Run pulls in parallel.** The point of this skill is to be fast; do not serialize the 6 data sources.
- **Cite sources.** Linear state from Linear, PR state from GitHub, worktree from local filesystem. Don't paraphrase one as another.
- **If the ticket isn't ours** (assignee ≠ owner@example.com), surface that in the header but still produce the report — it's read-only.
- **No invented data.** If a section has no data (e.g., no PR), say so explicitly. Don't fabricate "PR pending."

